# M14 "Open as": the kind the user names, not the one a name suggests.
# What each choice reads out, byte for byte, is pinned in tests/archive_helper.rs and
# tests/archive_vfs.rs: a clipboard transfer on this host answers later than one 20 s step of
# this script can span (measured 2026-11-11, docs/WINDOWS.md), so the reading stays there.

# The menu offers the container kinds that no name can tell apart.
open $T/w
select plain.img
expect-menu-item VeraCrypt / TrueCrypt
expect-menu-item dm-crypt (plain)

# A dm-crypt (plain) volume carries no header at all: nothing in the bytes says what it is, so the
# choice is the only door — and that choice asks for its passphrase before it reads a byte.
open $T/w
select plain.img
action win.open-as-volume DmCryptPlain
wait-dialog Passphrase for
dialog-entry Passphrase for = s3cret
dialog-button Passphrase for : Unlock
wait-row volume.img

# A VeraCrypt container under a name that says nothing: detection cannot reach it, the choice can,
# and the ask comes first — nothing is searched before an answer exists. Answered, the volume
# inside is listed.
open $T/w
select disk.bin
action win.open-as-volume VeraCrypt
wait-dialog Passphrase for
dialog-entry Passphrase for = test
dialog-button Passphrase for : Unlock
wait-row metadata.ini
wait-row volume.img

# Opening the same file again asks no second time: the session holds its passphrase.
open $T/w
select disk.bin
action win.open-as-volume VeraCrypt
wait-row metadata.ini

# A refused prompt is not a failed opening: the file opens without a passphrase, and a VeraCrypt
# reader with nothing to search answers the shell of a locked volume.
open $T/w
select locked.bin
action win.open-as-volume VeraCrypt
wait-dialog Passphrase for
dialog-button Passphrase for : Cancel
wait-row volume.img
wait-no-row metadata.ini

# A program answers the Archive entry with the resources inside it instead of being run,
# which is what its name alone would do.
open $T/w
select setup.exe
expect-menu-item Archive
action win.open-as-archive
wait-row MANIFEST
wait-row VERSION
